  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FAO Data for Healthy Diets Initiative - Informing actions to achieve healthy diets for all</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Provide diet-related data and statistics on FAO/WHO GIFT and Food  Diet Domain and ensure that they are accessed by global, regional and country stakeholders to identify diet-related issues, their potential causes and entry points to address them
2.Ensure that FAO/INFOODS and other platforms managed by FAO are up-to-date and accessed by global, regional and country stakeholders as the go-to data source for consistent and accurate information on food composition, including the contribution of food fortification 
3.Enhance the knowledge and capacity of global, regional and country stakeholders, and improve access to resources to enable the use of diet-related data for decision-making
4.Develop the evidence on healthy diet metrics among decision-makers and increase efficiency in resource use related to the measurement of healthy diets thus catalyzing their uptake in monitoring systems</narrative>
  </description>
